<title>USA: U.S. funding bill silent on CRP contract extension.</title>
<headline>U.S. funding bill silent on CRP contract extension.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The omnibus spending bill assembled in Congress would not allow the extension of Conservation Reserve contracts, an aide to House Agriculture Committee chairman Pat Roberts said Monday.</p>
<p>The bill was expected to receive final congressional approval later in the day.</p>
<p>Roberts, R-Kan., raised the idea last week of allowing extensions. He said proposed revisions in the Conservation Reserve Program would not treat the Great Plains fairly. He announced efforts last week to remove a ban on extending existing contracts.</p>
</text>
